 "nl": [
  "Allow scada to connect to vpn-users using MySQL (TCP 3306) and HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "Hosts in admin may reach iot-sensors over SSH (TCP 22).",
  "guest-wifi offers DNS over UDP 53 to every zone.",
  "Restrict library so that its only permitted destinations are scada on DNS over UDP 53; drop all other traffic it originates.",
  "hr is isolated: it may only reach database on HTTPS (TCP 443); guest-wifi on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Any zone may connect to cameras over HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "No packet from admin may enter voip, even for services open to everyone.",
  "cameras must accept PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) from monitoring.",
  "Deny all traffic from dns-servers to library (this overrides any public service).",
  "voip must never reach vpn-users, regardless of any other rule.",
  "voip must accept HTTP (TCP 80) and SSH (TCP 22) and SNMP (UDP 161) from iot-sensors.",
  "No packet from guest-wifi may enter admin, even for services open to everyone.",
  "cameras is isolated: it may only reach ops on NTP (UDP 123); guest-wifi on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Permit any TCP port from monitoring to library but deny Telnet (TCP 23), SMB (TCP 445), RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "Deny all traffic from mail to iot-sensors (this overrides any public service).",
  "Any zone may connect to library over DNS over UDP 53.",
  "Apart from ops on syslog (UDP 514), all traffic originating in voip must be dropped.",
  "Any zone may connect to research over HTTPS (TCP 443) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "admin must accept RDP (TCP 3389) and MySQL (TCP 3306) from dns-servers.",
  "vpn-users is isolated: it may only reach database on NTP (UDP 123); engineering on syslog (UDP 514), and nothing else.",
  "Deny all traffic from ops to iot-sensors (this overrides any public service).",
  "Apart from guest-wifi on DNS over UDP 53, all traffic originating in dns-servers must be dropped.",
  "Hosts in admin may reach voip over HTTPS (TCP 443) and syslog (UDP 514).",
  "Hosts in cameras may reach scada over syslog (UDP 514) and SMTP (TCP 25) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "ops may use TCP ports 1024-65535 towards engineering, except RDP (TCP 3389), which must be blocked.",
  "Hosts in database may reach hr over HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "Hosts in mail may reach hr over SNMP (UDP 161)."
 ],
